# Reverse away from a surface, far enough that whatever happens next does not drag the arm across
# it.
#
# It reverses and stops. It does not turn, and it does not walk anywhere: a navigation goal
# normally follows, and Nav2 is far better at going somewhere than a hand-rolled controller. The
# only job here is to get the base clear.
#
# Reverse tracks about as well as forward, the policy measuring -0.140 m/s at a commanded -0.20
# and -0.236 at -0.30, and shares the same deadband, so the server drives it above that floor.

# How far to end up from where it started, in metres. The gait coasts a little after the command
# stops, so expect to land slightly beyond it.
float64 distance_m
# Give up after this many seconds. 0 uses the server's own default.
float64 timeout_s
---
bool success
string message
float64 travelled_m
---
string PHASE_BACKING_OFF=backing_off
string phase
float64 travelled_m
